# Consumer-owned schema extension (issue 09 — Task content & time). The generated
# createComment / createAttachment / createTimeEntry CRUD mutations remain as
# low-level primitives on the Go client, but each raw GraphQL create exposes a
# concern a client must never own — so they are masked off the API (sqlgen.yml
# api.operations) and these blessed mutations are the write path instead:
#
#   * createComment trusts a client-supplied authorID — provenance the server
#     must own. commentOnTask stamps the author to the authenticated caller and
#     lets tenant scoping inject the Workspace.
#   * createAttachment trusts a client-supplied uploadedBy (server-owned) AND an
#     entityType/entityID pair that has NO foreign key (polymorphic, PRD §13.7),
#     so a raw create could point an attachment at any UUID in any Workspace.
#     attachToTask / attachToComment resolve the target tenant-scoped, then set
#     the discriminator and entity id themselves — a Task/Comment in another
#     Workspace is invisible.
#   * createTimeEntry trusts a client-supplied userID — the server-owned actor.
#     logTime stamps the caller and takes hours as a decimal quantity (story 34).
#
# This mirrors the blessed task mutations (issues 07/08) and the memberships /
# invitations masks. Resolver bodies live in task_content.resolvers.go and are
# preserved across `sqlgen generate` by gqlgen's copy-through semantics.

extend type Mutation {
  """
  Comment on a Task within the Active Workspace (PRD story 29). The author is the
  authenticated caller — never client-supplied — and the Task must be visible in
  the Active Workspace, so a Task in another Workspace cannot be commented on.
  """
  commentOnTask(taskID: UUID!, body: String!): Comment!

  """
  Attach a file to a Task within the Active Workspace (PRD story 33). The uploader
  is the authenticated caller; the polymorphic binding (entityType = task,
  entityID = the Task) is set server-side after resolving the Task tenant-scoped,
  so an attachment can never be pointed at a Task in another Workspace. The blob
  itself lives in external storage; this records its metadata.
  """
  attachToTask(taskID: UUID!, fileName: String!, contentType: String!, sizeBytes: Int!, storageURL: String!): Attachment!

  """
  Attach a file to a Comment within the Active Workspace (PRD story 33). As with
  attachToTask, the uploader is the caller and the polymorphic binding
  (entityType = comment, entityID = the Comment) is set server-side after
  resolving the Comment tenant-scoped, so a Comment in another Workspace is
  invisible.
  """
  attachToComment(commentID: UUID!, fileName: String!, contentType: String!, sizeBytes: Int!, storageURL: String!): Attachment!

  """
  Log a Time Entry against a Task in decimal hours (PRD story 34). The logging
  User is the authenticated caller — never client-supplied — and the Task must be
  visible in the Active Workspace. billable defaults to true and notes is
  optional.
  """
  logTime(taskID: UUID!, hours: Decimal!, spentOn: Time!, billable: Boolean, notes: String): TimeEntry!
}
